The map ofElement sends an information-system element of a neighbourhood basis to the filter of those system neighbourhoods that contain the basis neighbourhood of some token in the element's carrier. The underlying set of such a neighbourhood belongs to the system. The master set contains the bottom neighbourhood, and the bottom index lies in the carrier because the empty set entails it. For two such neighbourhoods, the witnessing indices form a consistent pair; exhaustiveness selects an index whose neighbourhood equals their folded intersection, the element is closed under that entailment, and that neighbourhood sits inside both. A larger neighbourhood keeps the same witness.
